# Security rules

- Validate every incoming body, query parameter and path parameter with Zod on the server.
- Client validation is for usability only; server validation is mandatory.
- Never trust client-supplied user ID, role, price, totals, stock, order status or permissions.
- Determine identity from the server-side session.
- Resolve role from trusted database data; public registration always creates a customer.
- Every admin API/service independently verifies admin role.
- RLS must be enabled on application tables and tested.
- Customers may access only their own profile, addresses and orders.
- Public catalog reads return active items only.
- Do not expose raw database errors, stack traces, secrets or tokens.
- Use safe, generic messages for unexpected errors.
- Rate-limit authentication and sensitive operations.
- Never log passwords, cookies, tokens, service keys, full request bodies or unnecessary personal data.
- Cookie-based mutations must have appropriate origin/CSRF protections.
- Checkout must re-read authoritative prices and stock, calculate totals server-side and use an atomic transaction.
